{
  "id": "q-stellar-recurring-payments",
  "question": "How should recurring or subscription payments be implemented safely on Stellar?",
  "surface": [
    "stellarDocs.search_wallet_dapp_docs",
    "skills.stellar-dev.dapp",
    "skills.stellar-dev.smart-contracts"
  ],
  "golden": {
    "answer": "Stellar has no native recurring-payment operation, and a past payment authorizes no future charge. Implement recurrence in the application or a contract-account policy: the user authorizes a scoped session or delegated signer limited to a named contract, asset, maximum amount, cadence and expiry, and a backend scheduler submits each charge. A token allowance is the other pull pattern: the payer approves a bounded amount and the charger calls `transfer_from`. Provide revocation, pause, idempotency and failed-payment handling; never take an unrestricted private key.",
    "keyFacts": [
      "Stellar has no native recurring payments; the app or a contract account schedules charges.",
      "A delegated credential should limit merchant, asset, amount, cadence and expiry.",
      "Users need revocation and pause controls, and never share unrestricted keys."
    ],
    "avoid": [
      "Do NOT claim Stellar automatically repeats a payment at a set interval.",
      "Do NOT say a subscription merchant needs the user's unrestricted private key."
    ]
  },
  "tags": {
